    "q-94473": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94473",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A data set has mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=16$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =2.5.$ Find the value of an observation that has $z$-score $z=-0.4.$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{¯}{x}=16,$ $z=-0.4,$ and $\\sigma =2.5$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\  & =16+(-0.4)\\cdot 2.5 \\\\  & =16-1 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
