    "q-332028": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332028",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A data set has a standard deviation $\\sigma =2.4$ and an unknown mean. An observation of the data set has the value $x=5.4$ and $z$-score $z=0.5.$ Find the mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{―}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5.4,$ $z=0.5,$ and $\\sigma =2.4$ into the formula and solving for $\\overset{―}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}+0.5\\cdot 2.4 \\\\ 5.4 & =\\overset{―}{x}+1.2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =4.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
