    "q-332239": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332239",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=3.08,{x}_{2}=8.68$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-1.2$ and ${z}_{2}=2.3,$ respectively. Find the mean $\\overset{¯}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{¯}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n3.08=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n8.68=\\overset{¯}{x}+2.3\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8.68-3.08 & =(2.3-(-1.2))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.6 & =3.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot 1.6 \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}-1.92 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
